      "materials": [
        {
          "week": 11,
          "title": "Basis and dimension",
          "notes": "A basis of a subspace H is a set of vectors in H that is linearly independent and spans H. Every basis of H has the same number of vectors: the dimension of H. To find a basis of Col A, row reduce A and take the pivot columns of the original A. The dimension of Nul A is the number of free variables. Rank theorem: rank A + dim Nul A = number of columns."
        },
        {
          "week": 12,
          "title": "Eigenvalues",
          "notes": "A nonzero vector x is an eigenvector of A if Ax = lambda x for a scalar lambda (the eigenvalue). To find the eigenvalues, solve det(A - lambda I) = 0. For each eigenvalue, the eigenvectors are the nonzero vectors in Nul(A - lambda I)."
        }
      ]
